From 0510c7d4f6b21ffd24b6a67caa29e09acaadea80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:22:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 28: make Unknown absorb the
 uniqueness-carrying join

The provenance lattice of the uniqueness-carrying analysis
(reussir-unique-carrying-recursion-analysis, run at -O aggressive) used
one value, `Unknown`, both for "no contributing path yet" and for
"provenance unknown". Its join treated `Unknown` as the identity, so a
value that is fresh on one path and unknown on another (a field loaded out
of a cell, an opaque call's result, a value shared by `rc.inc`) joined to
"fresh" and was proven unique. A self call on such a value went to a
`.unique` clone, whose `rc.assume_unique` became `llvm.assume(count == 1)`
on a shared cell, and LLVM then took the unique fast path: the clone
rebuilt the shared cell in place. A declaration's results (no returns)
were also `Unknown`, so a call to an external function contributed
nothing to a join either.

Split the two: bottom is the empty provenance set (no fresh bit, no
argument), the identity of the join, the start of a join over arms and
the optimistic start of a function summary in the fixpoint; `Unknown` is
top and absorbs the join. A declaration's summary is `Unknown` from the
start; every defined function's starts at bottom, so the Kleene iteration
is unchanged for code without unknown contributors.

Repro (tests/integration/frontend/unique_carrying_shared_field.rr): `f`
returns its argument on the base path and calls itself on `pick(..)`, a
fresh cell or `p.0`, a field of `p` that `p` still holds; at -O aggressive
`p.0` read 101 instead of 1 after the call (the clone's `bump` rebuilt it
in place). Now 1 at every level. The lit test
unique_carrying_soundness.mlir gains an opaque-call-or-fresh self call
(no clone, function not carrying) and a field-or-fresh result (not
carrying).
